            <div xml:id="d911">

                <pb facs="0857" n="847" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg847"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/2457: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-09T12:00:00+07:00">April 9,
                            1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 3:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your [<hi rendition="#italic">Shanghai’s</hi>] April 8, 4 p.m. I have today
                    written informally to the Foreign Minister pointing out the situation described
                    in your reference telegram and expressing the hope that the Chinese Government
                    will take steps to see that this threat to the peace and order of the
                    International Settlement is removed.</p>
                <p>Sent to Shanghai, repeated to Department, Peiping.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
